<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="safemode_help.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- safe mode wildcard help, monster names (HOSTILE_SPOTTED category). A passive
         backdrop stacked UNDER the string_input "Safe Mode Rule:" popup, replacing the
         curses help window. Static: no data model. Literal English with column
         alignment preserved (white-space: pre), matching the curses readout and the
         same i18n gap noted for the column heads. -->
    <div class="panel smh-panel">
        <div class="smh-text">* is used as a Wildcard.  A few Examples:

human          matches every NPC
zombie         matches the monster name exactly
acidic zo*     matches monsters beginning with 'acidic zo'
*mbie          matches monsters ending with 'mbie'
*cid*zo*ie     multiple * are allowed
AcI*zO*iE      case insensitive search</div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
